The root cause of the bug was the unnecessary introduction of the `prsctp_param` field in the `sctp_chunk` structure, which led to confusion and redundancy in managing expiration times for different prsctp policies. This resulted in incorrect handling of chunk expiration, particularly affecting the TTL policy and causing a performance regression in throughput. The coexistence of `prsctp_param` with other expiration-related fields created a situation where the logic for determining when to abandon chunks was inconsistent and inefficient.

Here is the patch:
  */
 struct sctp_datamsg *sctp_datamsg_from_user(struct sctp_association *asoc,
 					    struct sctp_sndrcvinfo *sinfo,
 					    struct iov_iter *from)
 {
 	int max, whole, i, offset, over, err;
 	int len, first_len;
 	int max_data;
 	struct sctp_chunk *chunk;
 	struct sctp_datamsg *msg;
 	struct list_head *pos, *temp;
